<title>RUSSIA: FOURTH RUSSIA SUGAR BEET CONTENT FALLS TO 10.4 PCT.</title>
<headline>FOURTH RUSSIA SUGAR BEET CONTENT FALLS TO 10.4 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's fourth sugar beet test, and the season's second for sugar content, showed a level of 10.4 percent from 11.0 percent at the same time last year, the Rossakhsvyokla sugar beet producers' association said on Friday.</p>
<p>It gave the following data:  </p>
<p>					     RUSSIAN SUGAR BEET TESTING</p>
<p>					 4th 1997 test     Year-ago level</p>
<p>					     Aug 1</p>
<p> Avg sugar content (pct)	     10.4		 11.0</p>
<p> Root weight (grams)		    205		  178</p>
<p> Daily root growth (grams)	    6.3		  5.1</p>
<p>The organisation did not give fresh data on the number of beets per hectare, adding that the next time such data would appear would be on August 20.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
